{"question": "请帮我判断远程办公审批路线，我还没有提供员工类别和每周天数，请先确认。
User reply: 我在试用期，每周只申请一天。", "answerable": true, "reference_answer": "Probationary employee needs HR approval even for one remote day.", "gold_evidence": [{"document_id": "428da73a353c42cab5f263ee9faaf873", "page": 7, "text": "REMOTE-26 current remote work policy: Regular employees may request up to two remote days per week with team lead confirmation. Requests above two days require an HR exception approval. Probationary staff require HR approval even for one day. A schedule does not constitute approval."}], "answer": "根据你自报的试用期身份和每周申请一天远程办公的情况，当前政策要求即使只申请一天也须获得HR批准；该判断以你的自报为条件，最终以HR批准为准。 [1] [5]

排班安排本身不构成远程办公批准。 [1]"}

{"question": "Calculate 3 notebooks at 1200 JPY each, and tell me the approval route under PROC-26. This is an estimate only.", "answerable": true, "reference_answer": "3600 JPY, within 5000 cap, requires prior manager confirmation and receipt; not approved.", "gold_evidence": [{"document_id": "428da73a353c42cab5f263ee9faaf873", "page": 1, "text": "PROC-26 current purchasing policy: Office supplies costing at most 5000 JPY per order require a receipt and manager confirmation before purchase. Orders above 5000 JPY require procurement approval before purchase. Splitting an order to evade this limit is prohibited. A calculation within the limit does not constitute approval."}], "answer": "The estimate is 3 notebooks × 1,200 JPY each = 3,600 JPY. [4] [5]

Assuming the notebooks are office supplies covered by the current PROC-26 policy, the 3,600 JPY estimate falls within the at-most-5,000-JPY-per-order route. [1] [4]

For that route, a receipt and manager confirmation are required before purchase; the calculation does not constitute approval. [1]"}

{"question": "My last working date is 2026-10-09. Calculate my RET-26 return deadline and list the materials. Do not claim I returned anything.", "answerable": true, "reference_answer": "2026-10-16 (7 calendar days after Oct 9), laptop charger return checklist asset ID; IT receipt unconfirmed.", "gold_evidence": [{"document_id": "428da73a353c42cab5f263ee9faaf873", "page": 6, "text": "RET-26 current equipment return policy: A departing employee must return the laptop and charger within 7 calendar days after the last working date. The return checklist and asset identifier are required. The seven-day calculation does not depend on business holidays. IT confirms receipt; a calculation cannot prove return completion."}], "answer": "Under the current RET-26 policy, the return deadline is 2026-10-16, calculated as 7 calendar days after your self-reported last working date of 2026-10-09. [1] [4] [5]

The required materials are the laptop, charger, return checklist, and asset identifier. [1]

The date calculation does not establish that the equipment was returned; IT confirmation is required to confirm receipt. [1]"}
